itbook.io/langchain-opentutorial/~gitbook/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fimg.shields.io%2Fbadge%2FOpen%2520in%2520GitHub-181717%3Fstyle%3Dflat-square%26logo%3Dgithub%26logoColor%3Dwhite&amp;width=300&amp;dpr=3&amp;quality=100&amp;sign=df43888b8282d1207893bcd2303dac3c&amp;sv=3\"/></span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 384 512\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"overflow:visible\" class=\"gb-icon ml-0.5 inline size-3 links-accent:text-tint-subtle\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M360 64c13.3 0 24 10.7 24 24l0 240c0 13.3-10.7 24-24 24s-24-10.7-24-24l0-182.1-295 295c-9.4 9.4-24.6 9.4-33.9 0S-2.3 416.4 7 407l295-295-182.1 0c-13.3 0-24-10.7-24-24s10.7-24 24-24l240 0z\"/></svg></a></span></p><h2 id=\"overview\" class=\"text-xl @xs:text-2xl @lg:text-3xl font-semibold heading font-heading pdf-heading block pr-6 pointer-fine:flex pointer-fine:items-baseline pointer-fine:pr-0 scroll-mt-(--content-scroll-margin) gb-align-start relative group/hash gb-block max-w-3xl w-full column-first-of-type:pt-0 pt-[1em]\" data-heading-reveal-wrapper=\"true\"><span data-cover-aware-text=\"\" class=\"pointer-fine:flex-1 z-1 justify-self-start max-w-full break-words page-cover-background:text-contrast-cover gb-align-start leading-tight\">Overview</span><span class=\"hash absolute [transform:translateY(0.125em)] pointer-fine:-ml-6 pointer-fine:relative pointer-fine:order-first pointer-fine:self-center pointer-fine:pr-2 pointer-fine:[transform:none] pointer-fine:[.flip-heading-hash_&amp;]:order-last pointer-fine:[.flip-heading-hash_&amp;]:ml-1 pointer-fine:[.flip-heading-hash_&amp;]:pl-2\"><a class=\"hash-link leading-tight\" aria-label=\"Direct link to heading\" href=\"#overview\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"overflow:visible\" class=\"gb-icon hash-icon size-4\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M226.9 29c2.8-13-5.5-25.7-18.4-28.5S182.7 6 180 18.9L156.6 128 68.5 128c-13.3 0-24 10.7-24 24s10.7 24 24 24l77.8 0-34.3 160-88 0c-13.3 0-24 10.7-24 24s10.7 24 24 24l77.7 0-21.2 99c-2.8 13 5.5 25.7 18.4 28.5s25.7-5.5 28.5-18.4l23.4-109 155.4 0-21.2 99c-2.8 13 5.5 25.7 18.4 28.5s25.7-5.5 28.5-18.4l23.4-109 88 0c13.3 0 24-10.7 24-24s-10.7-24-24-24l-77.7 0 34.3-160 88.1 0c13.3 0 24-10.7 24-24s-10.7-24-24-24l-77.8 0 21.2-99c2.8-13-5.5-25.7-18.4-28.5S387.2 6 384.4 18.9l-23.4 109.1-155.4 0 21.2-99zM195.4 176l155.4 0-34.3 160-155.4 0 34.3-160z\"/></svg></a></span></h2><p data-cover-aware-text=\"\" class=\"paragraph gb-block max-w-3xl w-full gb-align-start\">This tutorial explains how to use the <code class=\"py-px px-1.5 min-w-6.5 justify-center items-center ring-1 ring-inset ring-tint bg-tint rounded-sm text-[.875em] leading-[calc(max(1.20em,1.25rem))] break-words hyphens-none\">RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter</code>, the recommended way to split text in LangChain.</p><p data-cover-aware-text=\"\" class=\"paragraph gb-block max-w-3xl w-full gb-align-start\">The <code class=\"py-px px-1.5 min-w-6.5 justify-center items-center ring-1 ring-inset ring-tint bg-tint rounded-sm text-[.875em] leading-[calc(max(1.20em,1.25rem))] break-words hyphens-none\">RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter</code> works by taking a list of characters and attempting to split the text into smaller pieces based on that list. It continues splitting until the pieces are sufficiently small.</p><p data-cover-aware-text=\"\" class=\"paragraph gb-block max-w-3xl w-full gb-align-start\">By default, the character list is <strong class=\"font-bold\">[&#x27;\\\\n\\\\n&#x27;, &#x27;\\\\n&#x27;, &#x27; &quot;, &quot;&#x27;]</strong>, which means it recursively splits in the following order: <strong class=\"font-bold\">paragraph</strong> -&gt; <strong class=\"font-bold\">sentence</strong> -&gt; <strong class=\"font-bold\">word</strong>. This prioritizes keeping paragraphs, then sentences, then words together as much as possible, as these are considered the most semantically related units.</p><p data-cover-aware-text=\"\" class=\"paragraph gb-block max-w-3xl w-full gb-align-start\">Here&#x27;s a summary of how it works:</p><ol class=\"min-w-0 space-y-2 gb-block max-w-3xl w-full gb-block-list\"><li class=\"leading-normal flex items-start\"><div class=\"text-base leading-normal mr-1 flex min-h-lh min-w-6 items-center justify-center text-tint\"><div class=\"before:content-(--pseudoBefore--content) before:font-var\" style=\"--pseudoBefore--content:&#x27;1.&#x27;;--font-family:inherit;font-size:min(1em, 24px)\"></div></div><div class=\"flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col space-y-2\"><p data-cover-aware-text=\"\" class=\"paragraph gb-block max-w-3xl w-full min-h-lh [h2]:pt-0 [h3]:pt-0 [h4]:pt-0 mx-0 gb-align-start\">Splitting is done by a list of characters (<strong class=\"font-bold\">[‘\\\\n\\\\n’, ‘\\\\n’, ‘ “, ”’]</strong>).</p></div></li><li class=\"leading-normal flex items-start\"><div class=\"text-base leading-normal mr-1 flex min-h-lh min-w-6 items-center justify-center text-tint\"><div class=\"before:content-(--pseudoBefore--content) before:font-var\" style=\"--pseudoBefore--content:&#x27;2.&#x27;;--font-family:inherit;font-size:min(1em, 24px)\"></div></div><div class=\"flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col space-y-2\"><p data-cover-aware-text=\"\" class=\"paragraph gb-block max-w-3xl w-full min-h-lh [h2]:pt-0 [h3]:pt-0 [h4]:pt-0 mx-0 gb-align-start\">Chunk size is measured by the number of characters.</p></div></li></ol><h3 id=\"table-of-contents\" class=\"text-lg @xs:text-xl @lg:text-2xl font-semibold heading font-heading pdf-heading block pr-6 pointer-fine:flex pointer-fine:items-baseline pointer-fine:pr-0 scroll-mt-(--content-scroll-margin) gb-align-start relative group/hash gb-block max-w-3xl w-full column-first-of-type:pt-0 pt-[0.75em]\" data-heading-reveal-wrapper=\"true\"><span data-cover-aware-text=\"\" class=\"pointer-fine:flex-1 z-1 justify-self-start max-w-full break-words page-cover-background:text-contrast-cover gb-align-start leading-snug\">Table of Contents</span><span class=\"hash absolute [transform:translateY(0.17em)] pointer-fine:-ml-6 pointer-fine:relative pointer-fi